🔹 Types of Network Topology
1️⃣ Bus Topology

All devices are connected to a single cable (backbone).

📌 Advantage: Easy and cheap
📌 Disadvantage: If main cable fails, whole network stops

2️⃣ Star Topology

All devices connect to a central device (switch or hub).

📌 Most commonly used
📌 If one device fails, others still work
📌 If central switch fails, network stops

3️⃣ Ring Topology

Devices are connected in a circular form.

📌 Data moves in one direction
📌 If one cable breaks, network can stop (in basic ring)

4️⃣ Mesh Topology

Every device connects to multiple devices.

📌 Very reliable
📌 Expensive
📌 Used in large networks

5️⃣ Tree Topology

Combination of star + bus topology.

📌 Used in large organizations

🔹 Physical vs Logical Topology

Physical Topology → Actual cable connection

Logical Topology → How data moves inside the network

